# Student Marks & CSV Exporter (C++)

A small C++ practice project that stores a student's marks across five subjects, calculates the total and percentage, formats the record as a CSV line, and appends it to a local text file.

## What It Does
- Creates a `student` object with roll number, name, and marks for Maths, Physics, Chemistry, English, and Biology.
- Calculates total marks and overall percentage out of 500.
- Formats the student record into a comma-separated string using `ostringstream`.
- Appends the formatted record to a file (`58students.txt`) using `ofstream` in append mode (`ios::app`).

## Why I Built It
I wanted to practice combining basic OOP (classes and constructors), string stream formatting, and file handling in one small program instead of testing them separately.

## Known Quirks / Things to Fix
- The student details are currently hardcoded in `main()`.
- The output filename (`58students.txt`) and the console confirmation message (`students.txt`) do not match yet.
- `tocsv()` already includes a trailing newline (`\n`), while `main()` adds an extra `endl`.

